# release-please owns CHANGELOG.md and emits `*` bullets plus two blank lines
# after each heading. prettier collapses both, and a hook that modifies a file
# fails -- which would break the required Pre-commit hooks check on every
# release PR. prettier does not read markdownlint-configure-file directives, so
# the directive at the top of CHANGELOG.md does not cover this.
#
# Kept as its own entry even though `*.md` below now subsumes it: the reason is
# unrelated to table style and must outlive any future decision to hand markdown
# back to prettier.
CHANGELOG.md

# markdownlint owns markdown here -- see `table-column-style` in
# .markdownlint.yml. prettier can only emit *aligned* tables and offers no
# option to do otherwise, so letting it near markdown deadlocks the two hooks:
# prettier pads every cell, `markdownlint --fix` compacts them back, and each
# run reports "files were modified by this hook" forever.
#
# This file rather than the hook's `types_or` is the lever, because prettier's
# CLI and the VS Code extension both read it. A `types_or` change would leave an
# editor free to reintroduce aligned tables on save.
*.md
